      "side": 1,
      "message": "seems a little brittle to hard code 32 here, but we do have good comments and a panic, so we should catch any future code that breaks this assumptions pretty quickly.\n\nI don\u0027t have any suggestions that would allow us to avoid hard coding a number here. I think 1024 might be a little better since we should have enough ram for N mpu regions at 1K each and if a chip in the future has a larger minimum than 32, we won\u0027t break.\n\nI realize this is bike shedding at this point, so +2 either way.",
